    "created_at": "2022-01-13T21:40:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-15T02:20:41Z",
    "body": "``Set-PSReadLineOption -PromptText \"`e[1;32m❯`e[0m \", \"`e[1;35m❯`e[0m \"`` the problem is that the prompt varies depending on if the previous command failed or succeeded, that will mean we will have to run this at each call, but invoking starship again just to render the character module is likely not very efficient.\r\n\r\nAs in, just adding something like this into `global:prompt` won't be very efficient (Assuming we add support for `prompt --syntax-error`):\r\n```pwsh\r\nSet-PSReadLineOption -PromptText @(\r\n    Invoke-Native -Executable ::STARSHIP:: -Arguments @(\"module\", \"character\", \"--status=$($lastExitCodeForPrompt)\"),\r\n    Invoke-Native -Executable ::STARSHIP:: -Arguments @(\"prompt\", \"--syntax-error\")\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThough we can cache `prompt --syntax-error` like the continuation prompt, the character module varies depending on the exit code of the last command.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
